@jeromeschneider TOPS != TFLOPS. That's 275 TOPS of INT8 which you can't really use to train. And that machine only has 204.8 GB/s of RAM bandwidth vs 5760 GB/s (28x less)

Orin has 10.65 TFLOPS of FP16 (69x less)

7.5x cost increase for 28x RAM BW and 69x TFLOPS

@borggamingcloud 123 TFLOPS for 7900XTX. while 4090 is 330 for FP16-FP16 accumulate, this is pretty useless. for FP16-FP32 accumulate, it's only 165 TFLOPS, actually pretty close.

Also, the bottleneck is often RAM bandwidth and not flops. 960 GB/sec vs 1008 GB/sec.

The 7900XTX is better per $

